  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Integrated Vaccination against COVID-19 of Displaced Populations in the Provinces of Cibitoke, Makamba, Kirundo, Bujumbura and Mairie de Bujumbura Funded through COVID-19 Delivery Support (CDS3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to strengthen access to COVID-19 vaccinations for mobile populations by setting-up vaccination sites at five priority PoEs located in the provinces of Cibitoke, Bujumbura Rural, Bujumbura Mairie, Makamba and Rumonge. The specific goals are to: 1. Vaccinate against Covid-19 at least 5% of IDPs who are in host families, at least 5% of IDPs who are located in sites, and at least 10% of the target group of host family members in the targeted provinces; and 2. to catch-up at least 5% of children in the targeted provinces who have received zero doses or insufficient vaccinations as part of routine vaccination.</narrative>
  </description>
